# Set what this box is, without a screen.
#
# To use it: make a file called "alnasl-mode.txt" in this folder whose FIRST
# line is the word master or slave, and boot the Pi.
# This example does not count as it is: its first line is this comment.
#
#   master  runs the hall: Alnasl and the hall screen (the default)
#   slave   only reads DGT boards and passes them to a master: Arkab, no screen
#
# The file is read at boot and deleted. Nothing is erased: both keep their
# data, so switching back loses nothing. A slave is joined to its master on
# its own status page (http://<this box>:4050), once it is on the network.
